 "note": "Three passages over one mountain valley (DIV2K 0201). The SKY is combed into van Gogh's counter-rotating swirls with four placed centres and Starry Night's own colour distribution; the FERNS AND MEADOW are woven into Monet's short horizontal dabs; the LIMESTONE between them is left on the base grade, so the rock stays the thing the photograph says it is. A foveal map spends the stroke budget on the valley mouth rather than on the fern texture in the corners, which is where the content metric sends it unaided. Both masks are embedded, so this one file is the whole setup -- and it runs over any photograph, not only this one.",
